#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Spatial Cross-Validation for modelC (LGBM / RF / BRF)

Purpose: Perform spatial cross-validation by splitting Colombia into 4 spatial clusters
         (KMeans on standardized coordinates), training on 3 clusters and testing on 1 
         (rotating through all 4). Uses frozen benchmark features and hyperparameters.

Supported models:
  - lgbm: LightGBM (default)
  - rf: RandomForestClassifier
  - brf: BalancedRandomForestClassifier

Protocols:
  - pooled_years (default): Train and test on 2001-2017 mixed across folds
  - deployment_like: Train on non-heldout regions using 2001-2017, test on heldout region using 2018-2019

Memory optimizations:
  - KMeans clustering uses 10% sample for fitting, then assigns clusters in batches
  - Aggressive memory cleanup after each fold
  - Efficient batch processing during data loading

Input:   - modelC_{model_type}_win5_benchmark_*.json (most recent file from outputs/south_america/colombia/results/ml_models)
         - train_colombia_win5.parquet, earlystop_colombia_win5.parquet, test_colombia_win5.parquet

Output:  - Spatial CV results JSON with PR-AUC, P@1%, Lift@1% for each fold
         - Aggregated metrics across 4 folds
"""

